  "id": "COMPOUND:43698 - PROTEIN:5839",
  "verbalization": "Fluoranthene is shown to have a target relationship with Ataxin-2, which is further targeted by two distinct molecular entities: one is (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one, and the other is (2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-2-[2-(3,4-dihydroxy-5-methoxyphenyl)-7-hydroxy-3-[(2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxychromenylium-5-yl]oxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol. Both of these compounds share the common target Ataxin-2, which in turn is linked to U251. Additionally, Fluoranthene is also shown to target Oleamide, which also has a target relationship with U251. The evidence suggests that Fluoranthene may interact with Ataxin-2, potentially modulating its activity to affect U251. The mechanism of action is not fully elucidated, but the presence of multiple molecular entities targeting Ataxin-2 and U251 implies a possible regulatory or inhibitory pathway. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link between Fluoranthene and U251, though further investigation is needed to determine the exact nature of the interaction.",
